{"case_id":"C026","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration","input semantics"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["decoder.do_decode_frame","wuffs_base__image_decoder__decode_frame"],"reason":"H0 does not exercise the changed lower-quality, reduced-work-buffer decoding path. It never selects the configuration represented by `this.use_lower_quality`, and it always allocates `wuffs_base__image_decoder__workbuf_len(dec).max_incl`, so `args.workbuf` is not deliberately shortened to the range where `components_workbuf_offsets[8] > args.workbuf.length()`. The changed acceptance and `swizzle_immediately` behavior is therefore materially uncovered.","evidence":["The source change makes insufficient work-buffer handling depend on `(this.sof_marker >= 0xC2) or not this.use_lower_quality`.","The source change sets `this.swizzle_immediately = true` when the shortened-work-buffer path is accepted.","H0 only varies initialization flags and the output pixel format; no operation shown configures `use_lower_quality`.","`fuzz_image_decoder` obtains `wuffs_base__image_decoder__workbuf_len(dec).max_incl` and allocates exactly that amount whenever it is nonzero.","`decode_frame` is always called with that full `workbuf`, so H0 does not intentionally test shorter valid or boundary-length buffers around `components_workbuf_offsets[8]`."],"recommended_action":"Add a harness variant that enables the decoder's lower-quality configuration and calls `decode_frame` with fuzzed work-buffer lengths, especially immediately below, at, and above the relevant required-size boundary, across sequential and progressive JPEG inputs."}
